saving:
Nothing will know that you are gone,
Saving alone some sullen plough-land
None but yourself sets foot upon;

savage:
And where the wigwam stood the chapel stands;
The place that nurtured men of savage mien
Now teems with men of Nature's noblest types;

To rhyme the cry with which she still beats back
Those savage, hungry dogs that hunt her down
To the empty grave of Christ. The world’s hard pressed;

savings:
She never fell down and dirtied her knees;
She put all her pennies in savings banks;
She never omitted her "please" and "thanks";

saves:
Than another hue;
Saves she all of that for sunsets, --
Prodigal of blue,

saviour:
Should with full lustre in their conduct shine;
That Saviour, which his soul did first receive,
The greatest gift that ev'n a God can give,

saviour's:
It is something, yes, all, for us to stand
Clasping by faith our Saviour's hand;
To learn to labor, live and fight
